(FIL-21: an out-of-bounds list read sets the error flag and yields 0, and On error catches it; index 0 is out of bounds too, which is the 1-indexing claim from the other side.
 Also covers: FIL-22, FIL-23.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Extended 2026-10-05 (files batch C): appended rendered shapes of
 'gen leaf list out of bounds typed default' - a map holder, a list holder,
 a literal index into a number holder, and a text holder: each flags and
 reads its type's default.
 Ran (vox 0.4.15, 2026-10-05): VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-21.vox -o p && ./p
 exit code 0; actual output:
   Cannot access element 100 - out of bounds!
   0
   element 0 is out of bounds too
   0
   1
   0
   1
   0
   1
   0
   1
   FIL-21 empty text
)
